    "details": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<p>Next Bharat Ventures-Suzuki Innovation Centre is launching a pan-India Build Your Bharat Launchpad aiming to inspire bright young minds toward impact entrepreneurship across institutes in India, starting with IIT Hyderabad.</p>\n<p>Each campus co-hosts sessions on Impact Entrepreneurship and an 8-hour hackathon. The goal is to get the brightest students thinking about the problems faced by a billion Indians and building solutions for them.</p>\n<p>Winning teams receive ₹5 Lakhs (prize+grant) to kick-off their impact startup journey, access to expert mentorship, and an opportunity for up to ₹1 Crore in equity investment.</p>\n<p><strong>About the hackathon</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Themes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Agriculture: Increasing farmers' income</li>\n<li>Migrants Livelihood: Improving the livelihood of gig workers</li>\n<li>Rural Healthcare: Solving healthcare problems in small towns and rural areas</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Who can apply?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Students who want to build a startup</li>\n<li>Committed founders (students or recent graduates (2024-2026 batch) with a startup still in development)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Stages &amp; timeline</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Round 1 &ndash; Idea Submission [by Nov 8]\n<ul>\n<li>Submit an idea deck and a 3-5-minute video explaining your problem, solution and any ground work or prototype here</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Results &ndash; Shortlist announced [Nov 14].</li>\n<li>Hackathon &ndash; 8-Hour Hackathon (at SIC, IIT Hyderabad) [Nov 21]</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>What do winning student teams get?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>₹5 lakh (prize and seed grant)</li>\n<li>Up to ₹1 crore of investment in startup</li>\n<li>Mentorship</li>\n<li>Access to the living labs of Next Bharat's Impact Entrepreneurs</li>\n</ul>",
    "end_date": "2026-11-08T00:00:00+05:30",
